Props Alembic migrations
=======================

20260926000000 is the squashed, frozen final schema through the former chain's
last revision of the same name. A database already at that revision applies no
DDL or data changes. An older deployed database must first upgrade with an image
containing the old chain; never stamp it forward to hide missing migrations.

The baseline uses explicit Alembic/SQLAlchemy definitions for the final schema, without intermediate tables or
historical data rewrites. It preserves functions, triggers, materialized views,
constraints, RLS policies, grants, evaluator role setup and default privileges.
Fresh databases get a new agent-role salt and a populated (empty) examples view.
Downgrade-to-base retains the original baseline's destructive public-schema drop;
it is not a route back to an intermediate revision. No deployed DB is reset.

Dumps are independent test evidence, not migration code.

Provenance: schema-only CI artifact from the original chain at f481072738,
BuildBuddy invocation 529ec531-065b-5cdc-b113-51a1b6d56572,
//props/db/migrations:test_schema_baseline, test.outputs/props_schema.sql.
The original test compared a normalized dump digest against that independent
capture. The current test checks that an at-head upgrade preserves the schema
dump, object OIDs and salt, using only an isolated PostgreSQL testcontainer.

Future schema changes are ordinary child revisions. The squash equivalence check
is landing evidence, not a requirement to freeze this schema forever. Specimen
snapshots are not part of this migration tree.
